Prefer OpenRouter's authoritative billed cost over opencode's per-token estimate.

opencode 2.x prices every step as (catalog model rate x normalized token
counts) in SessionUsage.calculateCost and ignores OpenRouter's returned
usage.cost. For OpenRouter server-side tools like Fusion (a panel + judge + the
final answer = several completions across different models), and whenever
OpenRouter serves a request from a pricier endpoint than the catalog lists, that
undercounts and the displayed number bears no relation to what was billed.

The native OpenRouter route already requests usage accounting
(`usage: {include: true}` by default in packages/ai/src/providers/openrouter.ts
bodyOptions), and the raw usage block is kept on Usage.providerMetadata, but the
cost is never read: the OpenAI-chat mapper drops it from the typed Usage, and the
session runner's step settlement keeps only normalized tokens, so the raw usage
is gone by the time step.ts prices the step.

This is a backport of the source half of upstream anomalyco/opencode#52629
(open, unmerged at time of writing; tests omitted): add an optional
`Usage.cost`, fill it from `usage.cost` in the OpenAI-chat mapper, carry the raw
usage through the step settlement, and have SessionUsage.record prefer a finite,
non-negative reported cost, falling back to the per-token calculation. Providers
that do not report a cost leave Usage.cost unset, so this is a no-op for them.
Drop this patch once #52629 (or an equivalent fix for #43818) ships.

Verified with `git apply --check` against opencode v2.0.32. Not applicable to
1.x (the old 1.x patch targeted packages/opencode/src/session/session.ts).

